<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Benedetta of Cagliari</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1232 or 1233</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Benedetta was judge, or ruler, of the Judicate of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cagliari">Cagliari</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sardinia">Sardinia</a> from 1214 until her death around 1232. Her reign was dominated by the growing power of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pisa">Pisa</a>, which in 1216 built the fortress of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/castel-di-castro">Castel di Castro</a> on the hill above Cagliari. She struggled to preserve her independence through her marriages and appeals to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papacy">papacy</a>.</p></div>
